meta {
  name: Complete Registration
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/client/auth/complete-registration
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  name: Merdan Annagurdow
  city_id: {{city_id}}
  ~photo: @file()
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Merdan Annagurdow",
    "city_id": {{city_id}}
  }
}

docs {
  # Complete Registration

  Called after `verify-otp` when `is_new: true`. Saves the name, city and
  (optionally) the avatar.

  Worth doing before anything else: an order cannot be created without them,
  and the master application copies the name onto the master profile — an
  applicant with no name is rejected with `422`.

  **Body:** `multipart/form-data` when sending `photo`, plain JSON otherwise
  (switch the body type in Bruno — both are accepted).

  **Fields:**
  - `name` — required, max 255.
  - `city_id` — required, must exist in `cities`.
  - `photo` — optional avatar, `jpeg|png|jpg|webp`, max 5 MB. Converted
    **inline** (no queue) to WebP and downscaled to **512 px wide**, height
    proportional; images already narrower are not upscaled. Re-sending the
    endpoint with a new `photo` replaces the file and deletes the old one;
    omitting `photo` keeps whatever is stored.

  The saved path comes back as `client.photo` and the public URL as
  `client.photo_url`.

  **Response 200:** `ClientProfileResource`

  **Errors:**
  - `422` — name / city_id / photo validation error
  - `401` — missing or invalid token
}
